  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Raju Ramratan Mundada vs The Police Inspector on 12 February, 2019 Author: V.K. Jadhav Bench: V.K. Jadhav 1 Aba 16.2019.odt In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Bench At Aurangabad Anticipatory Bail Application No.16 Of 2019 Raju Ramratan Mundada Versus The Police Inspector ... Advocate for Applicant : Mr Chapalgaonkar Shailesh S. App for Respondent : Mr A P Basarkar ...",
    "facts": "The applicant is seeking pre-arrest bail in connection with Crime No.0315 of 2018 registered at Shillegaon Police Station, District Aurangabad for the offences punishable under sections 181, 272, 273, 328 of Indian Penal Code and u/s 59 of the Food and Safety Standards Act, 2006. His application with similar prayer bearing Criminal Bail Petition No.385/2018 came to be rejected by the Additional Sessions Judge, Vaijapur, District Aurangabad by order dated 21.12.2018. Said co- accused has taken name of the present applicant. Except this, there is no connecting evidence as against the present applicant.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel submits that, except the offence under section 328 of the IPC, other offences are bailable. Thus, there is hardly any evidence to the provisions of section 188 and 328 of IPC. Learned counsel submits that custodial interrogation of the applicant is not required. He may be released on anticipatory bail. 3. Learned APP has strongly resisted the application and submits that prima facie there are allegations in the FIR to attract the provisions of section 272 and 328 of the IPC. The applicants may not be released on anticipatory bail.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel submits that, except the offence under section 328 of the IPC, other offences are bailable. Thus, there is hardly any evidence to the provisions of section 188 and 328 of IPC. Learned counsel submits that custodial interrogation of the applicant is not required.",
    "respondent_arguments": "He may be released on anticipatory bail. 3. Learned APP has strongly resisted the application and submits that prima facie there are allegations in the FIR to attract the provisions of section 272 and 328 of the IPC. The applicants may not be released on anticipatory bail.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
